Purpose: Trim the platform data tables and per-LSP install logic to Linux and Android (Plan 0003, Section 5.4). In the LSP server definitions, every darwin and win32 download variant, executable suffix choice, and archive-format branch is deleted across all language servers (including the Python venv Scripts layout, the Eclipse JDT config switch, and the Clojure .exe lookup); Linux entries and behavior are preserved, and Android keeps its existing no-asset outcome. The ripgrep platform map keeps its two Linux entries, and the PowerShell-based zip extraction path is deleted with the zip entries it served.
Upstream files: packages/opencode/src/lsp/server.ts, packages/core/src/ripgrep/binary.ts
Rebase note: This is the fastest-moving file in the stack; upstream edits LSP definitions constantly. Rebase server by server: each definition keeps only its Linux download form. Watch for new servers that arrive with platform tables of their own.

